# Vanessa Automation Scenario Policy

## MUST

- Scenario relies on the task specification or an existing business case — no fictional flows
- One scenario = one observable behavior
- Before a new step, search for an existing one in the Vanessa library and the project scenarios
- The first scenario for a new case should be a short smoke test
- Scenario MUST run under a specific business user, not admin/AgentAI — exception only if the tested function is exclusively available to an administrator; determine the user from the task description, or **ask the human** if not specified

## SHOULD

- Specify the source: specification, task number, or the case being tested
- Move data preparation out of the main scenario
- Expectation should depend on the UI state rather than internal details

## Scenario source

- New task: based on the approved specification (before or alongside implementation)
- Implemented task: based on a real case (locking the regression)

## Anti-patterns

| Anti-pattern | Consequence |
|-------------|-------------|
| Invented flow without a project source | Does not protect a real requirement |
| Long scenario covering 5–7 meanings | Unstable, hard to diagnose |
| Checking internal details instead of behavior | Fragile scenario |

